@startuml
title TMFC035 : Party Roles & Permissions Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

' Unlike every other component's diagram of this type, this image contains NO
' eTOM Business Activity box at all -- consistent with the document body's
' section 2.1 ("eTOM business activities"), which has a header-only table
' with zero data rows: this component genuinely has no eTOM activity
' assigned. The diagram is, correspondingly, a pure SID-entity relationship
' view across three components, with no eTOM<->SID "produces"/"is consumed
' by" arrows anywhere in it. Reproduced as drawn, not forced to include an
' eTOM activity the source doesn't show.

package "TMFC035 - Party Roles & Permissions Management" {
  class "PermissionSet" as SIDPermissionSetA <<SID Data Entity>>
  class "PermissionSet" as SIDPermissionSetB <<SID Data Entity>>
  class PermissionSpecSet <<SID Data Entity>>
  class PartyRoleSpecification <<SID Data Entity>>
  class PartyRole <<SID Data Entity>>
}

package "TMFC028 - Party Management" {
  class Party <<SID Data Entity>>
}

package "TMFC020 - Digital Identity Management" {
  class DigitalIdentity <<SID Data Entity>>
}

' The source draws two separate cylinders both literally labelled
' "PermissionSet" side by side inside the TMFC035 box, linked to each other --
' reproduced exactly as two distinct entities with the same printed name, not
' merged into one (this may be a labelling artifact in the source PDF, but
' this redraw is of exactly what the image shows).

' All four links below are plain double-headed arrows (no legend-defined
' "produces"/"is consumed by" semantics -- that pairing is only defined for
' eTOM-activity<->SID-ABE arrows, and there is no eTOM activity in this
' diagram at all). Reproduced with plain, unlabeled double-headed arrows.
SIDPermissionSetA <--> SIDPermissionSetB
SIDPermissionSetA <--> PermissionSpecSet
PermissionSpecSet <--> PartyRoleSpecification
PartyRoleSpecification <--> PartyRole
SIDPermissionSetA <--> PartyRoleSpecification

' Cross-component links, each single-headed, direction as drawn:
' - PartyRole -> Party is drawn with a hollow/open triangle arrowhead (UML
'   generalization style), visually distinct from every other arrowhead in
'   this image, which are all solid/filled. That distinction is preserved
'   here rather than normalized away, though the source legend does not
'   define what the hollow style means.
PartyRole --|> Party
' - PartyRole -> DigitalIdentity and Party -> DigitalIdentity are both drawn
'   with ordinary solid, filled, single-headed arrows.
PartyRole --> DigitalIdentity
Party --> DigitalIdentity

legend right
  eTOM Business Activity = dashed rectangle (none appear in this diagram)
  SID Data Entities = cylinders (drawn here as classes for PlantUML)
  An arrow from an eTOM activity towards a SID ABE would mean the
  information is produced by the activity; the reverse would mean it is
  consumed by the activity -- not applicable here, as no eTOM activity
  appears in this diagram.
  The legend does not define meaning for arrows directly between SID
  entities or for the hollow-arrowhead link into Party; both are
  reproduced as plain, unlabeled connections with their drawn direction
  and arrowhead style preserved.
endlegend
@enduml
